    "path": "docs/programs/graph-policy-coordination-2026-10-18/README.md",
    "blob": "0dbff582a14c13e4b4b13cb1848a23b935d92697",
    "line": 15,
    "text": "Add an application-owned sidecar rather than changing `mw.training-export.v1` admission semantics. Record exact GP graph/program/checkpoint, feature projection, actor/selector, legal support at sample time, proposed vs admitted vs executed action, actual source receipt and final feedback status. Post-proposal admission is **not** original sampler support. Unknown/pending feedback cannot be invented as observed reward; global team outcome alone does not attribute causal benefit to each actor."
   },
   {
    "path": "docs/programs/graph-policy-coordination-2026-10-18.md",
    "blob": "01ff00d480ecd5e5f6999433612f0c713f1f72aa",
    "line": 16,
    "text": "6. Sidecar correlates observation, sampled decision and behavior log probability, resulting proposal, resolver verdict, source-owned effect receipt and external verifier outcome. Feedback corrections and promotion remain outside the policy's evaluation."
   }
  ]
 }
